    {
      "id": "GENUS_LASIORHINUS",
      "name": "Lasiorhinus",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Hairy-nosed wombats — two species with soft, silky fur over their muzzle (distinguishing them from the bare-nosed common wombat). The southern hairy-nosed wombat is the most abundant wombat species overall. The northern hairy-nosed wombat is one of Australia's most critically endangered mammals: it survives in a single location, Epping Forest National Park in Queensland, with fewer than 250 individuals — the population was down to just 35 animals in 1981. Conservation efforts have allowed gradual recovery, and a second population has been established at Richard Underwood Nature Refuge.",
      "lineage": "Wombats",
      "children": [
